WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were in business
for a long time

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.402 line:92%
before you were in television.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.636 line:92%
What is your take, you know,

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming from
the world of finance,

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.640 size:84% position:42%
is this idea of Trump
is a great businessman,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
is it a mirage or is there
something to the idea

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.079
that he was good at this other
thing before he was President?

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, if you were to compare
him to Mitt Romney,

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.283 size:78% position:39% line:92%
when Mitt Romney ran,

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
all of his peers
in private equity backed him.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.187 line:92%
When President Trump ran,

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.391
you didn't see anyone from
the big real-estate universe.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:27.694
You didn't see any big New York
business people back him.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:31.765
You saw people in middle America
who wanted a change.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:34.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the thing is
he did a brilliant thing

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.735 line:92%
in that he went to see them.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:39.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those rallies were in places
where I haven't visited.

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.807 line:92%
I don't know if you visited.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:41.808 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And it gave people hope.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
The twisted thing is
he gave them hope

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.646 line:92%
without an actual resolution.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:47.714 line:92%
He had the smarts to say,

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm gonna solve
income inequality,"

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:50.850 size:81% position:41% line:92%
but he's not doing it.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
When he says,
"I'm gonna go after trade,"

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.754 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that's a good idea.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.489 size:88% position:44% line:92%
There are issues. China?

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.524 line:92%
Yeah, there's problems there,

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:00.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
but what he's actually doing
makes no sense.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
If he said,
"Intellectual property

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.197 line:92%
or artificial intelligence,

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.231 line:92%
we're gonna go after that."

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:08.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
President Trump, if you asked
him about A.I., no joke,

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:11.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
he would think
it was a steak sauce.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.175 size:81% position:41%
-So what he's offering
the American people --

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:19.846 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:23.516
He's a brilliant marketer
with no real solutions,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.584 line:92%
and the country needs solutions.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.220
-You know, he falls back
on the economy every time

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.121 line:92%
it seems like he's cornered.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.123
Is there anything missing
because like you said,

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.792
consumer confidence is up, you
know, business confidence is up.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.096
Is there an argument to be made
that he's making a fair point

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he says,
"Hey, despite everything

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:41.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
and despite how it's a circus
at the White House,

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:41.901 size:78% position:39% line:92%
the economy is good,"

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is there something
that he's leaving out there?

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, there's something
to remember.

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:47.674
The economy was good before
President Trump took office.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:51.344
It was a slow and steady climb
out of the financial crisis.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.847
What Obama didn't do was sell it
very well.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.716 size:88% position:44%
He's a -- somewhat of a,
not a soft-spoken guy,

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
but certainly more humble
than Trump.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:00.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Everyone is.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And when Trump says
things are great

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's trickling down,
it's not.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:07.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have lots of people with
jobs, and that's great,

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they just don't pay
enough money.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.299
And so this idea that things are
going to trickle-down,

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.267 line:92%
if you look at Republicans

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.003
that are running for office now
in the midterms,

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
they don't talk about
the economy

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they know,
in their states,

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
people aren't living
comfortably.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.977 size:75% position:38%
It's those who don't
need to run again.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.880
They're saying, "Look at
this economy. It's great."

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.680 line:92%
It's great for big business.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.649
Right after Trump won --
I don't know if you remember --

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:33.219
he snuck out of Trump Tower and
he went to the 21 Club, right?

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.089
One of the fanciest restaurants
in New York.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.323 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Lots of people love it.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.424 line:92%
Filled with wealthy people,

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:42.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he said,
"I'm gonna lower your taxes."

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:42.562 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And he did.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
So President Trump
wanted to impress

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
and do this
for the wealthiest people

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:47.634 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and he has done that.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
The concern is that people
who voted for change

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.505 line:92%
aren't going to get that change.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I showed one of your greatest
hits, and again,

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a fan of your work,
but I do --

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's only fair
to show, really,

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.812 line:92%
one of the flubs of the year.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.181 line:92%
I have to tell you, I loved it.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were really happy
when you did it.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.084
-I'm glad you were.
My kids were too. My kids were.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.688
-This I will say, if your mom
was on TV and you were a kid,

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.889 line:92%
you'd be very happy about this.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:13.626
So here you are not as sharp as
you were earlier.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As California is farting --
excuse me -- fighting,

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:20.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
the largest wildfire
in the state's history...

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.804 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.439 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-They're farting.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:31.411
-Well, there are a lot of vegans
in California.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There are a lot of cleanses
that go on.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.015 line:92%
So they could be farting.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.617 line:92%
-They're farting the wildfires.

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:38.351 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-They could be farting.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:42.522
Listen, I did not get into
television until I was 36.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:48.161
So if you wanted a TV presenter
who is a teleprompter superstar

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
with perfect posture
and all of those things,

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.698 line:92%
then you picked the wrong girl.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:55.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I want, you know,
once a year

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone who accidentally
says farting.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-You know what?

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're gonna keep it real,
and you know, farting happens.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.776 size:84% position:42%
-It does happen. Thanks
so much for being here.

